    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1332-a2">

                <pb facs="0898" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg782"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Custom House circular.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Office of the Stamp Tax</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Head Office of the Stamp Tax, in Vera Cruz, in their circular No. 8, dated
                    the 3rd inst, advise me as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Department of Finance and Public Credit, in an order of this date,
                            advise me as follows:</p>
                        <p>“By order of the First Chief of the Constitutionalist Army, in charge of
                            the Executive Power, all companies or owners of mining lands or
                            petroleum explorations existing in this country, from this date must
                            make payments for Federal taxes to the respective Head Offices of the
                            Stamp Tax, under the Constitutionalist Government, or to the Head Office
                            of the Stamp Tax, at present located in this city, provisional capital
                            of the Republic; such payments as may be made to other authorities,
                            alien to this Government, <hi rendition="#italic">will be considered
                                null and void.</hi>”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>All of which I have the honor to transcribe to you for your information and
                    action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Guimbarda</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
